{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`caused_by` is the only machine-readable causation edge in the store, and it is not\ntrustworthy. `rebar link <bug> <target> caused_by` accepts ANY target: nothing checks the\ntarget is a change at all. The most-linked target today is a misattribution whose \"children\"\nare unrelated CI items, so `rebar metrics` (`bug_caused_by_fan_in`) and the epic-close\n`caused_by` floor (`llm/epic_bug_screen.py`) reason over edges nobody validated.\n\nVerified against `origin/main` before writing this plan:\n\n* `rebar link` validates only relation grammar, cycles, the redundant-link guard and the\n  closed-source guard (`graph/_links.py:add_dependency`), and has NO `--force`.\n* The \"does a commit reference this ticket?\" scan exists exactly once, privately, as\n  `_referencing_commits` in `_commands/close_precheck.py`; its `[]` return conflates\n  \"scanned, none found\" with \"no git history\".\n* `transition_close._apply_caused_by` writes its blame-derived edge via\n  `graph._links._write_link_event`, bypassing `add_dependency`: best-effort, out of scope.\n\n## Approach\n\n1. Hoist the trailer/subject scan into the existing shared module\n   `_engine_support/commit_impact.py` as `referencing_commits(ids, tracker, repo_root)`\n   returning `list[str] | None`, `None` = \"git history unreadable\" — the same `None`-vs-`[]`\n   distinction `changed_paths` there already uses. `close_precheck._referencing_commits`\n   becomes a thin `... or []` delegate KEEPING ITS NAME (a string monkeypatch target in\n   `tests/unit/test_attach_commits.py`); `_referencing_commit_exists` still delegates to it.\n2. Add ONE predicate, `caused_by_refusal(target_id, relation, tracker, code_root) -> str | None`\n   in `_commands/link_revert.py`, returning the refusal message or `None`. BOTH\n   `link_core` (the write) and `_link_dry_run` (the preview) call it, so the preview cannot\n   drift from the live refusal — `_link_dry_run` does not route through `link_core`, so a\n   shared predicate, not a shared code path, is what makes them one rule.\n3. The rule: for `caused_by`, the RESOLVED TARGET must have >=1 referencing commit.\n   The target ITSELF, not its descendants: `caused_by` must name the specific change that\n   introduced the defect, and crediting an epic through its children is the exact\n   misattribution this story exists to stop. `caused_by` is never hierarchy-promoted, so the\n   resolved target is the requested one.\n4. Placed in the command layer, not `add_dependency`: `rebar.graph` is the store layer, runs\n   NO git and takes no `repo_root` (only `tracker_dir`). `link_core`/`_link_dry_run` already\n   receive `repo_root` and `link_core` is `add_dependency`'s only functional caller. Both\n   resolve the CODE root as `config.repo_root(repo_root)` and pass THAT — never the tracker\n   dir, which an absolute `tracker.dir` can relocate outside the checkout — mirroring\n   close_precheck's `code_root`/`tracker` split.\n5. Unverifiable is NOT invalid: `None` from the scan (no code repo / no commits) allows the\n   link. A refusal must mean \"this target has no commit\", never \"this clone has no history\".\n6. Escape hatch `--force[=<reason>]` on the CLI, `force=` on library and MCP, spelled exactly\n   as `claim --force`. Its parser is hoisted to `_cli/_parsers/core/writes.py:extract_force`\n   and `claim._parse_force` delegates to it, so the spelling has one implementation.\n7. Oracle extensions AC-1 needs: a `\"link\"` branch in `write_parity_contract.execute()` (and\n   in `Case.op`), plus `link` on the Adapter protocol and all three adapters changed from\n   `(a, b, relation) -> None` to `(a, b, relation, *, force=None) -> Outcome`. Correcting an\n   earlier draft: `adapter.link` IS called, at `tests/interfaces/facades/test_parity.py:147`\n   (`test_deps_parity`), which discards the return value — that file joins Scope and gains\n   `assert adapter.link(a, b, \"blocks\")` so the new Outcome is checked rather than dropped.\n8. `SKILL.md` edit, co-located with the four attribution cases (~L633-644): the **Omission**\n   case attributes \"by scope-of-work rather than by introducing commit\" to a story/epic that\n   is commit-less by construction, which the new rule refuses. Worked example to add there:\n   `rebar link <bug> <story> caused_by --force=\"scope-of-work attribution: the story that\n   should have covered this case has no introducing commit\"`, plus the note that the forced\n   reason belongs in the RCA comment; the **Unattributable** case still leaves the link unset.\n\n## Scope\n\n`src/rebar/_engine_support/commit_impact.py`, `src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py`,\n`src/rebar/_commands/link_revert.py`, `src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/core/writes.py`,\n`src/rebar/_cli/help/link.txt`, `src/rebar/_commands/claim.py`,\n`src/rebar/_lib_mutations.py`, `src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py`,\n`tests/unit/test_caused_by_link_validation.py` (new), `tests/interfaces/adapters.py`,\n`tests/interfaces/write_parity_contract.py`, `tests/interfaces/facades/test_parity.py`,\n`docs/ticket-model.md`, `examples/agent-skills/rebar-debug/SKILL.md`.\n\n## Explicitly OUT of scope\n\nThe original plan's `introducing_sha` schema field + `rebar fsck` date check, and the\n\"attach the 196-row dated corpus\" criterion, are cut and re-filed as a follow-up linked\n`discovered_from`: no surface writes `introducing_sha` so the field would land dead; `fsck`\nis a STORE-integrity walker that must run where no code repo exists; the corpus is a review\nartifact absent from the repo.\n\n## Testing\n\nNew `tests/unit/test_caused_by_link_validation.py`, over a store whose code repo has real\ncommits: happy path (target carrying a `rebar-ticket:` trailer commit links); refusal (the\nerror names the target and `--force`, and `show_ticket(...)[\"deps\"]` is unchanged);\n`force=\"...\"` on the same input records the edge; `relates_to`/`blocks` to the same\ncommit-less target unaffected; a code repo with NO commits allows the link; `link --dry-run`\nprints a \"Would reject\" preview and writes nothing; `close_precheck._referencing_commits`\nstill resolves by name and still returns `[]` (not `None`) when history is unreadable.\n\nPinning: `tests/unit/test_attach_commits.py`, `tests/unit/test_caused_by_dedup_10d0.py`,\n`tests/unit/test_epic_bug_screen_4b54.py`, `tests/unit/test_close_gate_*.py`,\n`tests/unit/test_claim_*.py`, `tests/interfaces/facades/test_parity.py`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A `caused_by` link to a commit-less target is refused identically on library, CLI and\n      MCP, and `force` bypasses it on all three; checked by two new `op=\"link\"` rows in\n      `pytest tests/interfaces/test_write_parity_oracle.py -q`.\n- [ ] The refusal names the target and the escape hatch and leaves the store unwritten;\n      checked by `pytest tests/unit/test_caused_by_link_validation.py -q`.\n- [ ] `link --dry-run` on a commit-less `caused_by` target previews the refusal, and a code\n      repo with no commits allows the link; checked by the same command.\n- [ ] The scan has ONE implementation: `grep -cE '%H%x1f' src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py`\n      returns 0 and `grep -cE '^def _referencing_commits' src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py`\n      returns 1.\n- [ ] The close gate is behaviour-identical; checked by\n      `pytest tests/unit/test_attach_commits.py tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_completion_gate.py -q`.\n- [ ] `docs/ticket-model.md` states the rule and the `--force` hatch, and SKILL.md's Omission\n      case carries the forced-link worked example; checked by\n      `grep -c 'referencing commit' docs/ticket-model.md` returning >0 (0 today) and\n      `grep -c 'scope-of-work attribution' examples/agent-skills/rebar-debug/SKILL.md`\n      returning 1.\n- [ ] Gates green: `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and\n      `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` reporting `new=0 increased=0`.\n"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787415202332571001,"uuid":"0f74ed91-cd38-4a05-a41c-246d58e1cd56"}